[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "ruy-main 3.Bb5"]
[Name "3...Nge7: the Cozio Defence"]

3... Nge7 { The Cozio Defence. The knight guards c6, so that taking there wins nothing, but it blocks the f8 bishop. [%csl Yf8] }
4. O-O { Castles. The plan does not change. [%idea castle-early] }
4... a6
5. Ba4 { Stays on the diagonal. }
5... b5 6. Bb3 { The bishop looks at f7. [%cal Gb3f7] }
6... Ng6 { The knight has moved twice to free the bishop. }
7. c3 { The plan. d4 comes next. The sharper 7.d4 also works, but it needs exact moves. [%cal Gc3d4] }
7... Be7
8. d4 { Takes the centre. [%idea centre-pawns] }
8... O-O
9. Re1 { Every move has come from the same plan: castle, c3, d4, Re1. White has the centre and more space. [%cal Ge1e4] } *
